Add option_type=2 (eagle + 7988d) DMA/WED-hif2 routing support

Ports the option_type dispatch from MediaTek vendor feed
(0054-mtk-mt76-add-debug-tools.patch, commit d9334da8) onto upstream
mt76 b2704cf5, without the accompanying rro_bypass/txfree_path
refactor (not present in this base). Adds dev->option_type field,
reads it from the "option_type" DT property, and adds case-2 (eagle +
7988d dual-PCIe topology) branches to TXQ ring config, WFDMA host
config, RRO platform type, and wed_hif2 selection in
mt7996_register_phy() / mt7996_net_fill_forward_path().

Inert when option_type is unset in DT (falls through to default,
byte-for-byte equivalent to prior behavior). Verified empirically on
ASUS ZenWiFi BT8 (MT7988D, dual PCIe domains 0/2): insmod test with
this code but WITHOUT option_type set in DT showed TX PER of 5.9%
(15526 packets / 84 min), matching the prior confirmed baseline of
7.3% within normal day-to-day variance -- confirming the port
introduces no behavioral change on its own.

The option_type DT property itself (case-2 activation) is held back
pending UART-based verification, as a related change (wed_enable=1)
has caused a hard kernel panic on this platform; see project notes.

